=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources (web useTranslation only; controlled component): the parent props
    state / onExecute / onRequestDialog / onToggleFavorite / loading / lastStatus /
    isFavorite are bound through THREE P1/S8 seams — ToggleCommandDispatching (execute +
    requestInput, reporting ToggleCommandExecutionEvent started/succeeded/failed/offline),
    ToggleCommandFavoriteToggling, and ToggleCommandStateObserving (the live on/off the
    web reads as `state[def.stateField]`) — so ToggleCommandTileModel owns isOn / loading /
    lastStatus / isFavorite as derived state. No I/O in the view.
  - On/off resolution (web `isOn = def.stateField && state ? Boolean(state[field]) :
    localToggle`): ToggleStateProjection — bound toggles read the seam value (off +
    unresolved-loading until the first delivery, matching web reading false while `state`
    is null); unbound toggles track a local optimistic flip. Verified by 3 projection +
    4 model tests.
  - Activation (web `handleClick`): no-op while executing/offline; ON tap sends commandOff
    (guarded — no force-unwrap of `def.commandOff!`); OFF tap opens the dialog when the
    command needs input (web `inputConfig` → onRequestDialog) else sends the on command
    with its params (web onExecute). Unbound toggles flip localToggle on each tap.
  - Composition (web clickable GlassPanel + ghost Star Button + corner dot + Loader2/on-off Icon):
      • Tile     -> Button(.plain) + TSMaterial.panel glass; takes the variant tone fill +
                    border while ON (web onStyles.panel default→accent/danger→danger/success→
                    success); dims to 0.5 while executing (web `loading && opacity-50`); whole
                    tile activates (web onClick); subtle pointer-hover border (web hover:border-subtle).
      • Star     -> sibling overlay Button (independent tap = web e.stopPropagation()),
                    star.fill+warning tone when favorite else star+muted (web amber-300 / muted),
                    aria = web t('commands.toggleFavorite','Toggle favorite'); .isSelected trait.
      • State dot-> top-trailing Circle, variant tone while ON else muted (web `isOn ?
                    styles.dot : bg-surface-2`), decorative (accessibilityHidden).
      • Icon box -> ProgressView while executing else Image(systemName: iconName(isOn:)) — the
                    on/off symbol swap (web `isOn ? def.icon : def.iconOff ?? def.icon`); tinted
                    variant tone while ON (web onStyles.icon) else neutral surface box.
      • Label    -> label (textPrimary) + ON/OFF line (web t('commands.on'|'commands.off'),
                    variant tone while ON / muted, a spinner until a bound state resolves) +
                    status line (ToggleCommandOutcome → checkmark/exclamation glyph + tone, web
                    ✓ green / red).
  - States (ALL rendered; each has a #if DEBUG preview + a model/adapter unit test):
      loading (bound state unresolved → ON/OFF spinner) · off (resting, web OFF) · on (variant
      tone) · executing (icon spinner + dimmed, web loading) · succeeded (web ✓ green) ·
      failed (web red) · stale (freshness chip, time-based — native live-state chrome, ADR-013) ·
      offline (cached outcome kept + offline chip, activation blocked). Favorite on/off and the
      three variants are orthogonal modifiers. "empty" = the resolved-OFF resting tile (icon +
      label + OFF, never a blank box).
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved verbatim — "commands.toggleFavorite"="Toggle favorite",
    "commands.on"="ON", "commands.off"="OFF". Per-command label keys are dynamic (owned by the
    command catalog) and resolved through the same facade with the def's key+fallback (not
    redeclared). Native chrome keys namespaced commands.toggle.* (hint.turnOn/turnOff/configure,
    state.loading/sending/succeeded/failed, freshness.stale/offline). Referenced==declared
    verified: 12 surface-chrome keys referenced == 12 declared, 0 missing (the only 3
    referenced-not-declared are the dynamic command-label keys commands.climate.climate /
    commands.charging.charge / commands.security.sentry used in previews/fixtures, external
    by design). NO English string literals in native code (all via ToggleCommandTileStrings +
    Text(verbatim:)).
  - Accessibility: tile carries label (command) + value (on/off word + loading/sending/stale/
    offline/succeeded/failed) + hint (turn on / turn off / show options) + identifier
    (toggle-command-tile-<id>) + .isSelected when ON; favorite carries its own label +
